.TH WS-OBS 1 "2026-11-10" "ws-obs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ws-obs \- send OBS obs-websocket vendor requests, including browser-source input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ws-obs
[\fB\-\-url\fR \fIws://host:port\fR] [\fB\-\-password\fR \fIpass\fR]
\fIvendor\fR \fIsource\fR [\fItokens\fR...]
.br
.B ws-obs
[\fB\-\-url\fR \fIws://host:port\fR] [\fB\-\-password\fR \fIpass\fR]
.B call
\fIvendor\fR \fIrequestType\fR [\fIrequestData-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ws-obs
is a small obs-websocket v5 client. In the first form it speaks the
.B obs-browser-hid
vendor to send keyboard keys, text or mouse clicks to a named browser
source (or to the virtual sources
.B current
and
.BR interact ).
The second form sends an arbitrary
.B CallVendorRequest
to any obs-websocket vendor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-url " ws://host:port"
WebSocket endpoint. Defaults to
.BR ws://127.0.0.1:4455 .
.TP
.BI \-\-password " pass"
obs-websocket password, if authentication is required (flag or
.BR OBS_WS_PASSWORD ).
.SH TOKENS
.TP
.BI key
A key name (for example
.BR Return ,
.BR Escape ,
.BR F5 ,
.BR a ,
.BR Left ,
.BR space ).
.TP
.B Ctrl, Shift, Alt, Super, AltGr, NumLock, CapsLock
Modifier tokens before the key.
.TP
.BI \-\-up " key"
Send only the key release.
.TP
.BI \-\-down " key"
Send only the key press.
.TP
.BI \-\-text " string"
Type a whole string with the
.B SendText
request instead of keys.
.TP
.BI click " x y"
Left click at source-canvas position x,y.
.TP
.BI right-click " x y"
Right click.
.TP
.BI middle-click " x y"
Middle click.
.TP
.BI double-click " x y"
Left double click.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OBS_WS_URL
Default WebSocket URL.
.TP
.B OBS_WS_PASSWORD
Default obs-websocket password.
.TP
.B WSOBS_DEBUG
If set to a non-empty value, print raw response JSON to stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ws-obs obs-browser-hid current Return
Press and release Return on the first browser source in the program scene.
.TP
.B ws-obs obs-browser-hid interact ctrl c
Send Ctrl+C to the browser source whose interact window is open.
.TP
.B ws-obs obs-browser-hid browsersource2 double-click 120 80
Double-click at (120,80) in the source canvas.
.TP
.B ws-obs call vendor-foo DoThing '{"arg":1}'
Send a generic vendor request.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Connection, request or plugin error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad arguments, URL, password or oversized input).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR obs (1)
and the obs-websocket protocol documentation.
